{"schemaVersion":"1.0.0","kind":"eigenquestions-fine-index","destinations":[{"id":"source-question:4e321e90114dc6bb8af038135cfcb27a11aa41c8c409d80eaa0dbd9812f3bfaf","title":"Do anisotropic bulk solutions obey the same mass scaling, and can strong-coupling flux vacua be described by a tractable dual gauge theory? A separate unresolved task is to compute the correction coefficients that decide whether the proposed stabilization and uplift mechanisms work.","connectionCount":1,"detail":{"shardId":"destination-details-fine-0001"},"indexTemplate":"source_question"},{"id":"source-question:4e52ef2bd952088fc2e7ca6aa3be103a10eda6eb73493ddabccf8496fc8af981","title":"How does a large number of particle species constrain their mass scale and the gravitational cutoff, and could those constraints explain the weak/Planck hierarchy and require unusual microscopic black-hole decay patterns?","connectionCount":1,"detail":{"shardId":"destination-details-fine-0004"},"indexTemplate":"source_question"},{"id":"source-question:4ef10749b8b3fd847237a1a4d8167b98b8de3450ef23037094f80325d03bf4b4","title":"What geometry describes Euclidean vector multiplets coupled to gravity, how does temporal reduction define a local r-map, and how are scalar instanton actions related to lifted black-hole masses?","connectionCount":1,"detail":{"shardId":"destination-details-fine-0007"},"indexTemplate":"source_question"},{"id":"source-question:4e99cff7ccf946a11d8b7def17dab573760e10e10bcc1ba7e51bd34fe718e1d3","title":"Can the Adler-Bardeen R-current and the stress tensor belong to one quantum supercurrent despite their one-loop and multiloop anomalies? The paper also asks how equations of motion and infrared contributions enter proposed resolutions.","connectionCount":1,"detail":{"shardId":"destination-details-fine-0008"},"indexTemplate":"source_question"},{"id":"source-question:4e7fdce27fa1c114181feb3b0b3293cb8b41c1bf9acc4ad64315ebdcd7bd7b47","title":"Can type IIB LARGE Volume Scenario compactifications retain an uneaten QCD axion and additional ultralight ALPs after moduli stabilisation, and what couplings, cosmology and observational opportunities follow?","connectionCount":1,"detail":{"shardId":"destination-details-fine-0012"},"indexTemplate":"source_question"},{"id":"source-question:4eeddafc8e7ce573e7c5834ee53c89f9e8f2eff0d07b914e21f4a6c8e6f9fed6","title":"How much of the cosmological coincidence problem reflects the temporal parametrization used to display cosmic history, and what additional restrictions on the present matter/dark-energy ratio follow from structure formation and the ages of old stellar populations?","connectionCount":1,"detail":{"shardId":"destination-details-fine-0017"},"indexTemplate":"source_question"},{"id":"source-question:4eb174f9af4acad49657ffb05307bbad319e4477a1cb811d7c22470490cc876f","title":"Can the gauge-inflaton branch of an earlier five-dimensional conformal-SUGRA construction reconcile natural-inflation observables and the required horizon-exit e-fold count with its microscopic decay and reheating history? The analysis emphasizes unsuppressed tensor amplitudes and potentially very low reheating temperatures.","connectionCount":1,"detail":{"shardId":"destination-details-fine-0018"},"indexTemplate":"source_question"},{"id":"source-question:4e7765f4f9f4e397b94cafc5f3ba8f0e0a0d1ecb9a64e51f8e51428ba2abde7f","title":"Can kinetic and Stückelberg mixing produce an effectively super-Planckian axion decay constant from intrinsically sub-Planckian periodicities, without monodromy, decay-constant alignment or a large field multiplicity, while preserving gauge consistency?","connectionCount":1,"detail":{"shardId":"destination-details-fine-0018"},"indexTemplate":"source_question"},{"id":"source-question:4e98069672b0294b5fe963ebe5975fb22482c66dd31dea3c7b9ef23ab4a625f7","title":"Can exact field solutions on charged Nariai spacetime corroborate Hamilton–Jacobi tunneling for Hawking radiation, and what probability does the usual semiclassical emission factor represent?","connectionCount":1,"detail":{"shardId":"destination-details-fine-0021"},"indexTemplate":"source_question"},{"id":"source-question:4ebf97e737c69c0ef8fc8123fd7e44b326e95e12a4c963821ced77b397bcd178","title":"A stabilized type-IIB Kähler modulus must remain locally stable when positive supersymmetry-breaking energy is added. The baseline model combines a logarithmic Kähler potential, a flux constant, a single condensate exponential, and an anti-D3 energy proportional to the inverse square of the volume modulus.","connectionCount":1,"detail":{"shardId":"destination-details-fine-0028"},"indexTemplate":"source_question"},{"id":"source-question:4ea455d25f925a2ba8a956f05b4f002e50bf678ed2b309e51bd58ab2cfecd11e","title":"Can strongly coupled flux-monodromy effective theories realize technically natural quintessence with sufficiently small potential slope, controlled quantum corrections and observable departures from a cosmological constant?","connectionCount":1,"detail":{"shardId":"destination-details-fine-0033"},"indexTemplate":"source_question"},{"id":"source-question:4e8d650f770ee4df1d2bfcc209a892c736be694143c55968acec62cbf9488aa5","title":"Determine whether minimal gauge inflation can obey the refined de Sitter disjunction across its selected field branch and fit the quoted CMB inputs, thereby restricting the unknown universal constants c1 and c2.","connectionCount":1,"detail":{"shardId":"destination-details-fine-0034"},"indexTemplate":"source_question"},{"id":"source-question:4edabd93678f58a20bfe855ed6fe279dbb7d32299780701a9d17fb2bdc2f7253","title":"Do higher-level, differently gauged or apparently non-(2,2)-based heterotic constructions belong to the same network of orbifolds and interpolations? These cases test the universal connectedness conjecture beyond the explicitly discussed SO(10) toroidal families.","connectionCount":1,"detail":{"shardId":"destination-details-fine-0043"},"indexTemplate":"source_question"},{"id":"source-question:4ea928370f68b01d793f3ae3504f30847a429a59d4afb57ca8b2df36fb377fa0","title":"Which kinetic quantity measures weak gauge coupling, and how does it determine scalar distance? The full gauge matrix detects vanishing couplings through diverging eigenvalues, while scalar lengths use its pullback to fixed-volume tangent vectors.","connectionCount":1,"detail":{"shardId":"destination-details-fine-0055"},"indexTemplate":"source_question"},{"id":"source-question:4ed2ac936157aab2ac1031a731c7fd778188055e7092082eb69b67b68a11dc32","title":"Can high-scale supersymmetry and late string-modulus domination yield the observed abundance of superheavy neutralino dark matter, despite its overproduction in a standard thermal history, while remaining compatible with inflationary and dark-radiation constraints?","connectionCount":1,"detail":{"shardId":"destination-details-fine-0058"},"indexTemplate":"source_question"},{"id":"source-question:4ed65262ab8eef86382c7d02b813a2365001cf9c73093d15cf83039eea931d64","title":"Can a cosmological EFT containing a massive gravitino remain consistent after quantization of its longitudinal mode? The examples concern broken local supersymmetry, FRW evolution, and the constant-mass Rarita–Schwinger limit of supergravity.","connectionCount":1,"detail":{"shardId":"destination-details-fine-0063"},"indexTemplate":"source_question"},{"id":"source-question:4e56c73b94f158efc83139da35c385d32840dbd94461701f067b8650a4e29266","title":"What restrictions on D-dimensional particle spectra follow from requiring circle compactifications of Minkowski, de Sitter and anti-de Sitter vacua to satisfy the non-SUSY AdS and AdS Distance conjectures?","connectionCount":1,"detail":{"shardId":"destination-details-fine-0064"},"indexTemplate":"source_question"},{"id":"source-question:4ed0b0f5824966281a5c9a17e971e8cacd73a2ebdcb22bd17be0849a0780bcf8","title":"Can an electroweak-instanton axion simultaneously explain quintessence dark energy and the historically reported CMB polarization rotation, while satisfying anomaly cancellation, perturbativity and equation-of-state constraints?","connectionCount":1,"detail":{"shardId":"destination-details-fine-0066"},"indexTemplate":"source_question"},{"id":"source-question:4e1818c5cbe9e99a7018d8e987ed82fed05b22b4b08c5855d2a51b959ee71cc5","title":"How do six-dimensional bulk anomaly coefficients determine the anomalies of strings charged under self-dual tensor fields?","connectionCount":1,"detail":{"shardId":"destination-details-fine-0066"},"indexTemplate":"source_question"},{"id":"source-question:4eed395343818bfba203c6fb50a1692618ec3ad5b5c9c362928a4cb25d471ef7","title":"Can field redefinitions make the first string-curvature corrections analytically tractable for regular dilatonic black holes, including static solutions in arbitrary dimension and slowly rotating or accelerating solutions in four dimensions?","connectionCount":1,"detail":{"shardId":"destination-details-fine-0075"},"indexTemplate":"source_question"},{"id":"source-question:4eb6622fbf824c35058926edcc05c041691ceb5b4a9702a4c27ab70049b62d46","title":"Can the non-geometric part of toroidal O(d,d) symmetry be identified directly in the higher-dimensional supergravity action, constrain its couplings, and admit explicit first-order α′ corrections with an invariant action and closed transformation algebra?","connectionCount":1,"detail":{"shardId":"destination-details-fine-0076"},"indexTemplate":"source_question"},{"id":"source-question:4e41975077696b9111b99bb7665daebca9ae75ae68ac5e1d5fa1885f210a97eb","title":"How do known microscopic AdS5 end-of-the-world configurations realize dynamical cobordism in five dimensions, complete Karch–Randall branes with localized gravity, and extend to holographic theories with reduced supersymmetry?","connectionCount":1,"detail":{"shardId":"destination-details-fine-0082"},"indexTemplate":"source_question"},{"id":"source-question:4e1d627b47645506b8c047bb953f8a1a2cb95cfebaac48f5bb97daf0f424d2d1","title":"Assuming an axion is required for each Yang–Mills group, what cosmological and observable consequences follow for dark gauge sectors? The paper studies axion abundance, inflationary isocurvature, collective dilute stars, and intersector kinetic mixing in two concrete models.","connectionCount":1,"detail":{"shardId":"destination-details-fine-0083"},"indexTemplate":"source_question"},{"id":"source-question:4e6da10992c9480043b9a8f983e824628ed4851ac73f5dad6e846739671f5401","title":"How does torsion enter emergent Dirac-material geometry and fundamental gravitational theories, and what observable, inflationary or dark-sector effects are proposed?","connectionCount":1,"detail":{"shardId":"destination-details-fine-0084"},"indexTemplate":"source_question"},{"id":"source-question:4e6289f67de2c10e43e5dfbe9b3eda0b74a255bad45469e288f20cb9adce744a","title":"When do moduli-dependent brane tensions or particle masses generate geodesics through their logarithmic gradient flows, and when can this local spectral information identify trajectories approaching infinite-distance limits?","connectionCount":1,"detail":{"shardId":"destination-details-fine-0085"},"indexTemplate":"source_question"},{"id":"source-question:4e8aff51cfadc15ced0de3baa6d5794543d998151b82590318c26746e7a80cfb","title":"Under which critical-point parameter conditions can the authors' WGC charge-to-mass criterion coexist with a horizon-based WCCC criterion for RN-AdS black holes surrounded by perfect fluid dark matter, using EPST, RPST and boundary CFT thermodynamics?","connectionCount":1,"detail":{"shardId":"destination-details-fine-0087"},"indexTemplate":"source_question"},{"id":"source-question:4e2cab08e7f0df6be0448a25a839294e700e472b95d20785a81b881d554b05f1","title":"Can PFDM modify the horizon and extremality conditions of an asymptotically flat RN configuration so that Q > M remains compatible with the authors' Mild WGC criterion and with a singularity hidden behind a horizon?","connectionCount":1,"detail":{"shardId":"destination-details-fine-0087"},"indexTemplate":"source_question"},{"id":"source-question:4ea3981c7bacabc42813050df040b7a5dcd8c3f239caba4343b39cd2452bde9e","title":"Do cubic-interaction one-loop corrections remain perturbatively small in generalized E-type α-attractor models producing primordial black holes, and can their induced gravitational-wave spectra support a conditional reconstruction of the inflationary potential?","connectionCount":1,"detail":{"shardId":"destination-details-fine-0092"},"indexTemplate":"source_question"},{"id":"source-question:4eae345baff7f3f762cac1d839e7a7e0b2cecff610df749d327c5cc10dd53e84","title":"Does the proposed quadratic-action prescription define a positive metric along arbitrary paths in multi-parameter families of AdS vacua, and how should it handle moduli and finite-range solution directions?","connectionCount":1,"detail":{"shardId":"destination-details-fine-0093"},"indexTemplate":"source_question"},{"id":"source-question:4e46e8a6e98d00a4b93a3d78291fea1340276a1f49811129d1d7ba403c007d88","title":"Does physically separating visible matter and supersymmetry breaking on different branes enforce a sequestered Kähler potential, suppress tree-level scalar masses, and make anomaly mediation a generic solution to the supersymmetric flavor problem?","connectionCount":1,"detail":{"shardId":"destination-details-fine-0108"},"indexTemplate":"source_question"},{"id":"source-question:4ed0c278eba787413e97fee4849282fbda1369771fb53b7e1244e27d40e5c2c9","title":"Can codimension-two braneworlds be created within the no-boundary proposal, what are their semiclassical creation probabilities and entropies, and can their entropy exceed the conjectured positive-cosmological-constant N-bound?","connectionCount":1,"detail":{"shardId":"destination-details-fine-0111"},"indexTemplate":"source_question"},{"id":"source-question:4ecd4b5e6fc56c1a4cfa49d4f5aa9c740b22f6419ed43a2951fdcf9fb264d03b","title":"How do closed-string fluxes support four-dimensional type II vacua, constrain internal geometry, generate effective potentials and stabilize moduli? The review also examines corrections, proposed de Sitter constructions and statistical distributions of vacua.","connectionCount":1,"detail":{"shardId":"destination-details-fine-0114"},"indexTemplate":"source_question"},{"id":"source-question:4ef40fc75357132f351e7b8958adb569e5803344fef42b39053c139088d8bbed","title":"Can many-cycle smooth horizonless geometries reproduce the charges and angular momenta of maximally spinning three-charge BPS black holes, connect continuously to zero-entropy black-ring configurations, and provide a countable microstate degeneracy?","connectionCount":1,"detail":{"shardId":"destination-details-fine-0115"},"indexTemplate":"source_question"},{"id":"source-question:4eebe154936413b733bc12534815c3befec10c830c404e3e6945db1ccb610b2b","title":"Which rank assignments make finite-string-coupling brane box models consistent, and how do string consistency conditions distinguish worldvolume gauge anomalies from scale anomalies and NS5-brane bending?","connectionCount":1,"detail":{"shardId":"destination-details-fine-0120"},"indexTemplate":"source_question"},{"id":"source-question:4ebf031a9cff6d598723f1e32307c4e64774a524655021ee1a2431ded10c6d0e","title":"How can a second law remain meaningful for an exterior observer when a body carrying ordinary entropy disappears through a horizon?","connectionCount":1,"detail":{"shardId":"destination-details-fine-0121"},"indexTemplate":"source_question"}],"relations":[{"id":"source-access:fa1b4193c2e3d90b607840c4","source":"q025-candidate-region:45f6412f0b685bf8bf595207","target":"source-question:4e321e90114dc6bb8af038135cfcb27a11aa41c8c409d80eaa0dbd9812f3bfaf","detail":{"shardId":"relation-details-0039","recordSha256":"d8e79eff069476089b3d6dd4e58025236a8258fcec0cc22abc9f728afbc05f5e"},"indexTemplate":"source_question"},{"id":"source-access:0b4425799711676f613eaad7","source":"q025-candidate-region:ace45537f56681cc78d7a950","target":"source-question:4e52ef2bd9520